WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.201
-Thank you very much, everyone!

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:03.870
Thank you!
On a Friday!

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:07.439
That's some Friday love
right there.

00:00:07.439 --> 00:00:09.609
Thank you. Welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:11.277
Let's get to the news
and jokes.

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:12.812
Well, guys, everyone's
still talking about

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.747
last night's
presidential debate.

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:16.248
But based on the early ratings,

00:00:16.248 --> 00:00:19.785
it had about 7 million fewer
viewers than the first one.

00:00:19.785 --> 00:00:22.388
It's not that 7 million people
chose not to watch.

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:25.358
It's that after the first
debate, they left the country.

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:27.327
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:30.263
Based on some snap polls,
Trump won the debate

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:33.600
by 98% to 2%.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.835
That's according to
the fair polling site,

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:38.204
guntotingeagle.com.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:40.139
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.139 --> 00:00:41.941
But this is interesting.
The Trump campaign announced

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.944
that yesterday was their biggest
online fundraising day ever,

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:47.346
pulling in $26 million.

00:00:47.346 --> 00:00:51.417
Wow, he really has the
bird-killing wind at his back.

00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:53.620
Yep, Trump raised $26 million.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:56.355
Today he was like,
"Spend the million on TV ads,

00:00:56.355 --> 00:00:58.191
put the rest in my
Chinese bank account."

00:00:58.191 --> 00:01:00.560
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.562
Did you see this?
Two of Trump's guests last night

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.930
were Kid Rock
and golfer John Daly.

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:06.732
Take a look at this.

00:01:06.732 --> 00:01:09.168
[ Laughter ]
They look great.

00:01:09.168 --> 00:01:11.971
I think they bought those
clothes at QAnon Members Only.

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:14.840
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.943
Yep, Trump wanted Kid Rock's
support, mostly because

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:19.479
he thinks Kid Rock is
Dwayne Johnson's son.

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:22.615
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.550
I shouldn't make fun of them.
In 2024,

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.486
that's going to be
the Republican ticket.

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:27.753
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:29.956
Meanwhile, after the debate,
Donald Trump Jr.

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:31.825
went on Fox News and he was
really pumped

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:33.025
about his dad's performance.

00:01:33.025 --> 00:01:35.928
I mean, really pumped.
Watch this.

00:01:35.928 --> 00:01:38.597
-The media runs right away.
It's Russian disinformation.

00:01:38.597 --> 00:01:40.099
There's literally zero evidence

00:01:40.099 --> 00:01:41.734
that it's Russian
disinformation.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.602
The Director of National
Intelligence said --

00:01:43.602 --> 00:01:45.471
and by the way, more
importantly, the FBI said it,

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:47.907
and I don't say that because
I think the FBI has more

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:51.677
credibility, I say that because
it's pretty clear that the FBI

00:01:51.677 --> 00:01:54.447
has done whatever they possibly
could to hurt Donald Trump.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:56.983
So if they're even coming out
and saying this,

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.417
meaning the upper levels
of the FBI.

00:01:58.417 --> 00:01:59.919
The door kickers love us,

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:02.088
not so much the bureaucrats
at the top.

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:06.993
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:09.495
-Okay.

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:11.497
Was he double parked
or something?

00:02:11.497 --> 00:02:17.170
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:18.804
Looks like someone's been
dipping into Daddy's

00:02:18.804 --> 00:02:21.807
nuclear-powered steroids.

00:02:21.807 --> 00:02:23.375
He sounds like a kindergartner

00:02:23.375 --> 00:02:24.910
who can't wait to tell you
about his day.

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:26.512
And then -- and then --
and then we finger painted,

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:28.381
and then we ate lunch,
and then we played outside,

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.416
and then we -- and then
we stuck up for Russia,

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.084
and then --

00:02:32.084 --> 00:02:33.853
I didn't know if I was
watching "Hannity"

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:35.421
or an episode of "Narcos."

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:38.090
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.326
In six months, Don Jr.'s
going to be auctioning off

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:41.995
unclaimed storage units.

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:45.564
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.564 --> 00:02:47.099
That was a good deep cut.

00:02:47.099 --> 00:02:49.201
He sounds like the guy who reads
the side effects

00:02:49.201 --> 00:02:50.670
on the end of
a Zoloft commercial.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:54.040
[ Rapid indistinct talking ]

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:57.210
Sounded like every conversation
that's ever happened at a rave.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:03:00.980
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.881
Well, with less than two weeks
until the election,

00:03:02.881 --> 00:03:05.318
the President is campaigning
as much as he can.

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:06.952
Take a look.
-President Trump,

00:03:06.952 --> 00:03:10.456
he is about to begin a whirlwind
weekend of campaigning.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:13.259
He'll be heading down South for
campaign events in the villages,

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:16.062
then a rally tonight in the
Panhandle and Pensacola.

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:18.064
He'll be staying overnight
in Florida, getting a chance

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:19.798
to early vote tomorrow.

00:03:19.798 --> 00:03:21.901
He'll be holding rallies this
weekend in places like

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:24.503
North Carolina, Ohio,
and Wisconsin.

00:03:24.503 --> 00:03:27.807
And then Sunday, another rally
in New Hampshire.

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:29.475
-He's starting to turn
into that band where

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:31.644
you're just like,
"Weren't they just here?"

00:03:31.644 --> 00:03:33.379
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:35.014
The rallies aren't
really changing

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:36.382
Trump's approval rating.

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:38.951
However, the coronavirus numbers
are through the roof.

00:03:38.951 --> 00:03:40.820
[ Laughter and ohhs ]

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:43.356
Trump hasn't worked this hard
since he had to be quiet

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:45.291
for two minutes at the debate
last night.

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.592
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.592 --> 00:03:47.894
This is pretty crazy.

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:50.162
A security researcher claims
that he was able to

00:03:50.162 --> 00:03:53.532
get into Trump's Twitter account
by guessing his password.

00:03:53.532 --> 00:03:55.033
Check out what it was.

00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:57.270 line:0%
-A Dutch security researcher
was able to access

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:59.238 line:0%
President Trump's
Twitter account last week

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:01.207 line:0%
by guessing his password,

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:03.109 line:0%
maga2020!

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:06.446
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:08.747
-If you're worried about
the nuclear codes, don't be.

00:04:08.747 --> 00:04:12.285
That password is maga2020!!
with two exclamation points.

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:14.053
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:15.822
Well, another big story is
early voting.

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:17.223
Millions of Americans
are doing it,

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:19.058
and today one of them
was Mike Pence.

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:21.794
Here he is casting his ballot
in Indiana.

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.429
Yep, the Pences were excited.

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:26.031
They haven't done a joint
thumbs up since their honeymoon.

00:04:26.031 --> 00:04:33.940
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:37.610
"What do you think?"
"All right."

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:40.179
Some news from overseas.

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:42.014
-Okay.

00:04:42.014 --> 00:04:43.315
Never mind.

00:04:43.315 --> 00:04:45.784
-Some news from overseas.
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:45.784 --> 00:04:48.754
-North Korea has ordered
a lockdown over concerns that

00:04:48.754 --> 00:04:52.058
yellow dust from China could
spread the coronavirus.

00:04:52.058 --> 00:04:53.659
Kim Jong-Un made
the announcement,

00:04:53.659 --> 00:04:55.961
along with his infectious
disease expert,

00:04:55.961 --> 00:04:57.964
Dr. Kim Jong-Fauci.

00:04:57.964 --> 00:05:01.734
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:03.135
If the lockdown wasn't
bad enough,

00:05:03.135 --> 00:05:04.603
Kim Jong-Un is now
forcing everyone

00:05:04.603 --> 00:05:06.438
to do a Zoom happy hour.

00:05:06.438 --> 00:05:10.143
[ Sighs ]
Gosh.

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:12.044
If you think quarantine
in America is bad,

00:05:12.044 --> 00:05:14.113
over in North Korea, the only
thing they have on Netflix

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:16.415
is "Emily in Pyongyang."

00:05:16.415 --> 00:05:20.519
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.519 --> 00:05:22.021
-Nice one.
-You can give me a thing.

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:23.422
-I got it.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:23.422 --> 00:05:25.390
It's just a mental -- it's
a silent [imitates rimshot].

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:26.625
-I got it.
-It's alright.

00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:28.261
[ Rimshot ]
No, no. That's right.

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:30.162
That's hacky. I know.
You don't want to do that.

00:05:30.162 --> 00:05:31.464
-I take it back.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:33.199
-[ Imitates reverse speaking ]

00:05:33.199 --> 00:05:34.867
-Oh, he took it back.
-Yeah.

00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:36.702
-Oh, my God.
[ Applause ]

00:05:36.702 --> 00:05:39.338
-He actually reversed
himself.

00:05:39.338 --> 00:05:42.341
He reversed himself.
That was awesome.

00:05:42.341 --> 00:05:45.545
[ Imitates reverse speaking ]

00:05:45.545 --> 00:05:47.479
Hey, did you see last night
the New York Giants

00:05:47.479 --> 00:05:49.615
were playing...some team.
-Who?

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:53.852
-[ Groaning ]
-It doesn't matter, right?

00:05:53.852 --> 00:05:55.521
The Philadelphia Eagles.

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:58.524
-Yeah.
[ Rimshot ]

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:02.794
-And Giants quarterback
Daniel Jones tried running

00:06:02.794 --> 00:06:04.930
for an 88-yard touchdown.

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:06.232
Let's see how that went.

00:06:07.866 --> 00:06:10.336 line:0%
-From the 12. Jones keeps.

00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:12.004 line:0%
Gets a block.

00:06:12.004 --> 00:06:15.608 line:0%
Takes off, and he is gone!

00:06:15.608 --> 00:06:18.110 line:0%
Trying to stay upright,
and he trips!

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:20.847 line:0%
[ Gasping ]
[ Rimshot ]

00:06:20.847 --> 00:06:24.484
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.484 --> 00:06:25.851
-That felt like re-watching

00:06:25.851 --> 00:06:27.186
the last season
of "Game of Thrones."

00:06:27.186 --> 00:06:28.921
Like, yes, yes...aw!

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:30.923
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:32.357
Well, the holidays
are coming up,

00:06:32.357 --> 00:06:34.727
and Southwest Airlines just made
a big announcement

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:36.395
about their flights.
Take a look.

00:06:36.395 --> 00:06:38.864 line:0%
-Southwest Airlines is
dropping a pandemic policy

00:06:38.864 --> 00:06:41.767 line:0%
that provided more social
distancing on flights.

00:06:41.767 --> 00:06:44.202 line:0%
It will no longer keep
middle seats empty,

00:06:44.202 --> 00:06:45.838 line:0%
starting December 1st.

00:06:45.838 --> 00:06:48.507 line:0%
Southwest says air filtering
and masks

00:06:48.507 --> 00:06:52.144 line:0%
have created healthy
environments aboard planes.

00:06:52.144 --> 00:06:54.680
-Come on.
It's Southwest.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.449
The whole plane is
a middle seat.

00:06:56.449 --> 00:06:59.651
[ Laughter ]

00:06:59.651 --> 00:07:01.253
You actually don't have
to worry,

00:07:01.253 --> 00:07:02.821
because even the coronavirus
doesn't want anything to do

00:07:02.821 --> 00:07:04.924
with the middle seat on
Southwest.

00:07:04.924 --> 00:07:06.525
The middle seat on Southwest.

00:07:06.525 --> 00:07:09.595
I'd rather be on lockdown
in North Korea.

00:07:09.595 --> 00:07:11.363
Pretty sure the only in-flight
entertainment they have

00:07:11.363 --> 00:07:13.766
on Southwest is
"Emily in Pyongyang."

00:07:13.766 --> 00:07:15.834
[ Laughter ]

00:07:15.834 --> 00:07:19.371
[ Scattered applause ]

00:07:19.371 --> 00:07:21.807
And finally, Guinness
is about to unveil

00:07:21.807 --> 00:07:24.276
its newest product.
Let's see what it is.

00:07:24.276 --> 00:07:27.179
-Guinness launching its
first-ever non-alcoholic beer.

00:07:27.179 --> 00:07:28.981
It's called Guinness Zero.

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:31.984 line:0%
It took the company four years
to re-create the same taste

00:07:31.984 --> 00:07:34.720 line:0%
as its original stout
without the alcohol.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.956
-If you order that
in Ireland,

00:07:36.956 --> 00:07:38.723
you're marched through
town while everyone throws

00:07:38.723 --> 00:07:40.525
rotten vegetables at you.

00:07:40.525 --> 00:07:42.561
"Shame, shame!"

00:07:42.561 --> 00:07:45.030
[ Laughter ]

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:46.298
Guinness without booze?

00:07:46.298 --> 00:07:48.067
Here's how Irish people
are reacting.

00:07:48.067 --> 00:07:49.335
-Come on!
-There you go.

